<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE starlink-15-16 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 Starlink Group 15-16 (27 V2 Mini Optimized, SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 10.16 s, kick 3.769 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.400, payload 16909 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.4473-0.000934*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: SpaceX Falcon 9 Block 5 (reusable first stage, droneship recovery) — TIMELINE mode (sim/vehicles/falcon9.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Falcon 9 Block 5 masses from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9 Block 5&#x27; spec table; thrust/Isp from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9&#x27; spec table (citing SpaceX).
TIMELINE mode (tuned 2026-10-25): MECO 146 s, stage sep 150 s, SES-1 156 s, fairing 176 s, SECO-1 (final cutoff) from SpaceX&#x27;s sl-15-16 timeline are hard events.
Throttle profile not published: full published thrust throughout; unburned stage-1 residual stands in for entry/landing propellant.
Not flown: LL2 NET 2026-10-27T04:45Z (Mon Oct 26 9:45 pm PDT), status Go; Spaceflight Now agrees (B1082.26, OCISLY). File ends at SECO-1 (parking orbit); SES-2/deploy not simulated.
Published timeline (SpaceX): Max-Q 1:08, MECO 2:26, stage sep 2:30, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:56, SECO-1 8:39, SES-2 53:01, SECO-2 53:03, deploy 1:01:53.
Target orbit: SpaceX pre-launch state vector (CelesTrak SupGP starlink-g15-16): deploy 252 x 265 km, i 70.007 deg. Deploy epoch 05:47:17Z = T+1:02:17 vs SpaceX page 1:01:53 (24 s, noted).
Target (see launch config): insertion 159 km, apoapsis 265 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 155.45 deg; payload 16909 kg.
Pad: 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-10-27T04:45:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
